$ MacNeal & Harder (1985), Sec. 7 - Scordelis-Lo roof.
$ Cylindrical roof, radius R = 25, length L = 50, thickness t = 0.25,
$ subtended angle 80 deg, supported on rigid diaphragms at the two ends.
$ E = 4.32e8, nu = 0.0. Self-weight loading via GRAV.
$ Quarter model exploiting two symmetries:
$   x = 0   : midspan symmetry plane (xz section)
$   phi = 0 : circumferential symmetry plane (xz section at top)
$ Mesh 4x4 = 16 CQUAD4 over the quarter, 5x5 = 25 nodes.
$ Reference vertical displacement at the midspan/free-edge corner:
$   Uz at node 5 = -0.3024  (downward).
$
SOL 101
CEND
TITLE = MacNeal-Harder Scordelis-Lo roof (quarter model, gravity)
SUBCASE 1
  LABEL = Self-weight 4x4 mesh
  SPC = 1
  LOAD = 1
  DISPLACEMENT = ALL
BEGIN BULK
$ ---- solver parameters ----
$ Drilling-DOF stabilisation is not part of the benchmark definition and
$ solvers default it differently (MSC/Nastran 70.5 SOL 101: 0.0; MSC.Nastran
$ 2004+ and OpenJFEM: 100.0). Pinned so the accuracy and same-deck parity
$ comparisons are parameter-exact. See validation/README.md, "PARAM,K6ROT".
PARAM,K6ROT,0.
$ ---- material and property ----
MAT1, 1, 4.32+8, , 0.0, 1.0
PSHELL, 1, 1, 0.25, 1
$ ---- grids: 5 along arc (phi = 0, 10, 20, 30, 40 deg) by ----
$ ----        5 along length (x = 0, 6.25, 12.5, 18.75, 25)  ----
$ Coordinates: y = R*sin(phi), z = R*cos(phi).
$ Row 1: x = 0 (midspan)
GRID,  1, , 0.00,  0.00000, 25.00000
GRID,  2, , 0.00,  4.34120, 24.62019
GRID,  3, , 0.00,  8.55050, 23.49231
GRID,  4, , 0.00, 12.50000, 21.65063
GRID,  5, , 0.00, 16.06969, 19.15111
$ Row 2: x = 6.25
GRID,  6, , 6.25,  0.00000, 25.00000
GRID,  7, , 6.25,  4.34120, 24.62019
GRID,  8, , 6.25,  8.55050, 23.49231
GRID,  9, , 6.25, 12.50000, 21.65063
GRID, 10, , 6.25, 16.06969, 19.15111
$ Row 3: x = 12.5
GRID, 11, ,12.50,  0.00000, 25.00000
GRID, 12, ,12.50,  4.34120, 24.62019
GRID, 13, ,12.50,  8.55050, 23.49231
GRID, 14, ,12.50, 12.50000, 21.65063
GRID, 15, ,12.50, 16.06969, 19.15111
$ Row 4: x = 18.75
GRID, 16, ,18.75,  0.00000, 25.00000
GRID, 17, ,18.75,  4.34120, 24.62019
GRID, 18, ,18.75,  8.55050, 23.49231
GRID, 19, ,18.75, 12.50000, 21.65063
GRID, 20, ,18.75, 16.06969, 19.15111
$ Row 5: x = 25 (diaphragm end)
GRID, 21, ,25.00,  0.00000, 25.00000
GRID, 22, ,25.00,  4.34120, 24.62019
GRID, 23, ,25.00,  8.55050, 23.49231
GRID, 24, ,25.00, 12.50000, 21.65063
GRID, 25, ,25.00, 16.06969, 19.15111
$ ---- elements (4x4 grid) ----
CQUAD4,  1, 1,  1,  6,  7,  2
CQUAD4,  2, 1,  2,  7,  8,  3
CQUAD4,  3, 1,  3,  8,  9,  4
CQUAD4,  4, 1,  4,  9, 10,  5
CQUAD4,  5, 1,  6, 11, 12,  7
CQUAD4,  6, 1,  7, 12, 13,  8
CQUAD4,  7, 1,  8, 13, 14,  9
CQUAD4,  8, 1,  9, 14, 15, 10
CQUAD4,  9, 1, 11, 16, 17, 12
CQUAD4, 10, 1, 12, 17, 18, 13
CQUAD4, 11, 1, 13, 18, 19, 14
CQUAD4, 12, 1, 14, 19, 20, 15
CQUAD4, 13, 1, 16, 21, 22, 17
CQUAD4, 14, 1, 17, 22, 23, 18
CQUAD4, 15, 1, 18, 23, 24, 19
CQUAD4, 16, 1, 19, 24, 25, 20
$ ---- midspan symmetry (x=0): Ux = Ry = Rz = 0 ----
SPC1, 1, 156, 1, THRU, 5
$ ---- top symmetry (phi=0, the y=0 line): Uy = Rx = Rz = 0 ----
SPC1, 1, 246, 1
SPC1, 1, 246, 6
SPC1, 1, 246, 11
SPC1, 1, 246, 16
SPC1, 1, 246, 21
$ ---- rigid diaphragm at x = 25: Uy = Uz = Rx = 0 (in-plane fixed) ----
SPC1, 1, 234, 21, THRU, 25
$ ---- self-weight: rho * g = 360 in -z, so q = 90 per unit area ----
GRAV, 1, 0, 360.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.0
ENDDATA
